   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Instant Photo\n\nAn instant-photo frame with a handwritten caption. The photo is a built-in live placeholder (a drifting sunrise gradient); layer your own video or image over the photo window to use it.\n\nCategory: ui-blocks. Length: 5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- Media belongs in a hand-placed instant-photo frame with a handwritten caption.\n- A live scene should keep playing inside a stop-motion paper scene.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You just need a plain rounded frame with no paper story: use backdrop with padding.\n- The card needs to wobble or sit at an angle: wrap it with paper-wobble and place it yourself.\n\nVariables:\n- caption (string): Caption, default \"first light\"\n- caption_at (number, 0-60): Caption starts, default 0\n- width (number, 320-900): Card width, default 652\n- caption_size (number, 20-56): Caption size, default 36\n- frame_color (color): Frame, default \"#fdfcf8\"\n- caption_color (color): Ink, default \"#26242c\"\n- step (number, 1-6): Frames per pose, default 3\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
